From 2e7d96df9d07a53cf7d635e5e2468d1ea99d610f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 09:28:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] Fix two validation verdicts found by end-to-end testing

Running collect_validation.sh against simulated hosts in both credential
modes, as a real telegraf user with a venv, surfaced two ways the report
could mislead:

- audit_stats_interval.py reported "Intervals diverge" (exit 1) when a UCS
  domain could not be reached. A failed query proves nothing either way.
  It now exits 2 with "Not verified" when no domain disagreed but some could
  not be queried, and only exits 1 on an actual mismatch.
- The collector copies and the UCSM audit inherited the proxy variables of
  the admin's shell. On SUSE, /etc/sysconfig/proxy commonly exports
  https_proxy, so validation would route through a proxy that production
  never uses and report reachable domains as down. Network-facing runs now
  drop the shell's proxy variables and take the telegraf service's own,
  from `systemctl show -p Environment telegraf`. Verified with a stubbed
  service environment: HTTPS_PROXY is honored, NO_PROXY hosts go direct.

Also: the report summary now carries the before/after result (lines,
malformed lines, exit codes). shellcheck clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016getrRJmgohzHoA5TH2zVQ
(cherry picked from commit d92912a241114fc64765c2984f165588292fe7e7)
---
 tools/audit_stats_interval.py | 41 +++++++++++++++++-----------
 tools/collect_validation.sh   | 50 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 2 files changed, 67 insertions(+), 24 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tools/audit_stats_interval.py b/tools/audit_stats_interval.py
index 5209a5c..3e09b74 100755
--- a/tools/audit_stats_interval.py
+++ b/tools/audit_stats_interval.py
@@ -28,7 +28,8 @@ Usage (credentials from either mode, see credsource.py):
     (default: /etc/telegraf/telegraf.conf and /etc/telegraf/telegraf.d).
     -d names a dashboard JSON to read [[polling_interval]] from.
 
-Exits 0 when the intervals agree, 1 when they diverge, 2 on an error.
+Exits 0 when the intervals agree, 1 when they diverge, 2 when they
+could not be verified (a UCS domain unreachable, bad credentials, bad args).
 """
 
 # Kept compatible with Python 3.6, which is what the CentOS 7 UTM VM ships:
@@ -264,7 +265,7 @@ def main():
         print(f"error: {exc}", file=sys.stderr)
         return 2
 
-    all_agreed = True
+    queried, failed, diverged = 0, 0, 0
